# newdoc id = texts/birchbark/907
# date_created = 1100-1120
# transl_ru = Грамота от Тука к Гюряте. Крали-то братнины холопы, [крали] у брата. А теперь он (хозяин дома), сговорившись с родственниками, свалил [всё] на эту кражу, вместо [того, чтобы объявить] о той краже. А у него (в его ведомстве) действительно украдено, ан ведь он взял (за свое молчание) у Иванкова смерда три гривны, а кражу княжеского имущества скрыл.
# transl_en_1 = Message from Tuk to Giuriata. It’s the peasants (kholopy) of the brother who stole, [stole] from the brother. And now he (the owner of the house), having conspired with the neighbors, blamed it all on this theft, instead [of declaring about] that (other) theft. And he, indeed, had [the knowledge of] the theft, since he took (for his silence) from Ivanko’s peasant (smerd) three grivnas, and he concealed the theft of the prince’s items.
# transl_en_2 = [Outer side] A letter from Tuk to Gjurjata. The brother’s serfs have stolen, (they have stolen) from his brother. And now he (the landlord) has plotted with the relatives; he has shifted (everything) on this theft, instead of (telling about) that theft. And from him (in his district) there has been stolen indeed, but in fact he has taken from Ivanko’s peasant three grivnas and has concealed the theft of the princely property. [Inner side] And from him […]
